istry coherently with evidence.\n6|\n7|Every new/refined selector, TLS mutual-host authentication, credential lifecycle and versioned migration obligation must map to its real implementation owner. Inspect the approved coordinator recommendation and source contract. Unsupported runtime behavior remains truthfully uncovered; catalogue adoption does not implement TLS or selectors. Use board commands for ownership/task changes, never direct .task-board writes. Preserve all unresolved acceptance obligations and human-only epic isolation. Add a concrete task checklist before implementation.\n8|\n9|Use Go testing skill and repository gates. Run CI only locally, never enable or start hosted CI. Tests must drive real consumers, including negative behavior. Prior producer mutation-battery evidence had masked failures and restoration issues; independent reviewer recovered six true kills. Record individual command exit codes, use isolated mutation copies, restore byte-exact, and require semantic assertion failures. Compile errors, unapplied mutations, missing tools, empty test selections and pipeline-masked failures are not kills. Add an instrument positive control when claiming mutation evidence.\n10|\n11|Publish a task-board CR and hand off to independent review. Do not integrate or land before review. Keep task-scoped outcome with actual command exits and scope limits. All commits signed as configured Ivan Oparin; no broad destructive Git operations. This final leaf must make the whole Story's adopted source actually consumed while accurately distinguishing pending runtime implementation.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
