{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e139","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08707-ceef-7493-9b49-24effd76d285"},"sequence":3831,"recorded_at":1780531400007657,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"89c3b30b-a554-4b21-8bbd-183ab5ebf7c3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"89c3b30b-a554-4b21-8bbd-183ab5ebf7c3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"89c3b30b-a554-4b21-8bbd-183ab5ebf7c3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"87370ed8-230c-4311-b9b4-74266b6bfaa0"},"task_id":"87370ed8-230c-4311-b9b4-74266b6bfaa0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"87370ed8-230c-4311-b9b4-74266b6bfaa0","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-161-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git diff HEAD -- internal/traceability/traceability.go internal/specpin/pin.go | head -n 140; echo; tail -n 20 LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Review traceability diff and logbook style\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"diff --git a/internal/specpin/pin.go b/internal/specpin/pin.go\\nindex 908803f..d9e69b8 100644\\n--- a/internal/specpin/pin.go\\n+++ b/internal/specpin/pin.go\\n@@ -41,11 +41,12 @@ const (\\n // The v0.6.0 constants below adopt the independently accepted signed release\\n // agent-session-manager-spec v0.6.0 (annotated tag object\\n // 40c123eb8399efa8e05cbc009110940ed861a785 peeling to commit\\n-// 0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6) as an additional pinned source.\\n-// Every v0.5.0 constant above keeps its historical meaning: nothing here\\n-// relabels the old lock, document, or inventory, and Current/Verify still\\n-// serve the v0.5.0 baseline the catalogue and traceability gates consume\\n-// until the owning follow-up task re-points them.\\n+// 0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6) as the adopted normative source\\n+// authority. Every v0.5.0 constant above keeps its historical meaning: nothing\\n+// here relabels the old lock, document, or inventory. Current/Verify still\\n+// serve the v0.5.0 baseline for the intentionally-historical platform-path\\n+// registry; the catalogue, traceability, and CI gates consume v0.6.0 through\\n+// CurrentV060/VerifyV060 and derive the historical projections from it.\\n const (\\n \\tReleaseV060 = \\\"v0.6.0\\\"\\n \\tTagV060     = \\\"v0.6.0\\\"\\n@@ -151,14 +152,21 @@ func BytesV060() []byte {\\n \\n // Current returns a newly decoded copy of the embedded, verified release pin.\\n //\\n-// Current still serves the v0.5.0 baseline: the catalogue and traceability\\n-// gates verify the v0.5.0 lock file and document, and they keep doing so\\n-// until the owning follow-up task regenerates them against v0.6.0. Callers\\n-// that need the adopted v0.6.0 authority use CurrentV060.\\n+// Current still serves the v0.5.0 baseline: the platform-path registry in\\n+// internal/localstore binds that historical source explicitly through\\n+// CurrentV050. Catalogue, traceability, and CI gates consume the adopted\\n+// v0.6.0 authority through CurrentV060 instead.\\n func Current() (Manifest, error) {\\n \\treturn Verify(embeddedPin)\\n }\\n \\n+// CurrentV050 is the explicit historical v0.5.0 baseline reader. It is the\\n+// binding intentionally-historical consumers declare, so a future change to\\n+// what Current serves cannot silently re-point them at a newer authority.\\n+func CurrentV050() (Manifest, error) {\\n+\\treturn Verify(embeddedPin)\\n+}\\n+\\n // CurrentV060 returns a newly decoded copy of the embedded, verified v0.6.0\\n // release pin: the adopted normative source authority.\\n func CurrentV060() (Manifest, error) {\\ndiff --git a/internal/traceability/traceability.go b/internal/traceability/traceability.go\\nindex 3056626..1a32c3d 100644\\n--- a/internal/traceability/traceability.go\\n+++ b/internal/traceability/traceability.go\\n@@ -29,9 +29,9 @@ import (\\n )\\n \\n const (\\n-\\townershipRegistryPath = \\\"internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json\\\"\\n-\\tcontractLockPath      = \\\"internal/specpin/v0.5.0.lock.json\\\"\\n-\\tcatalogMetadataPath   = \\\"internal/catalog/catalog.v0.5.0.json\\\"\\n+\\townershipRegistryPath = \\\"internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json\\\"\\n+\\tcontractLockPath      = \\\"internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json\\\"\\n+\\tcatalogMetadataPath   = \\\"internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json\\\"\\n \\tgeneratedCatalogPath  = \\\"internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go\\\"\\n \\n \\townershipFormat        = \\\"ax-spec-to-code-ownership\\\"\\n@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ const (\\n \\t// reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 pins the semantic JSON projection. JSON\\n \\t// formatting may change, but ownership claims cannot be self-minted without\\n \\t// an explicit review of this binding.\\n-\\treviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 = \\\"caaca4c9b2d0a2ddb225810dba757807474230cf20e39cb3676c902f83fd9faa\\\"\\n+\\treviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 = \\\"81a29888e5ce9313fdc14dc9180f7c363a68195c6013e90023f626b66631b5be\\\"\\n )\\n \\n var ErrTraceability = errors.New(\\\"spec-to-code traceability check failed\\\")\\n@@ -89,7 +89,7 @@ type ownershipRegistry struct {\\n \\tUnownedSections []unownedSection `json:\\\"unowned_sections\\\"`\\n }\\n \\n-// unownedSection records a real v0.5.0 section that this repository does not\\n+// unownedSection records a real v0.6.0 section that this repository does not\\n // implement. It exists so an unimplemented section is disclosed by name rather\\n // than bound to a symbol from a neighbouring package, which is what an owned\\n // key would otherwise assert. It is a disclosure, never an exemption: a section\\n@@ -223,7 +223,7 @@ func verifyRepository(repository fs.FS, assignedSections []string) (Report, erro\\n \\tif err != nil {\\n \\t\\treturn Report{}, err\\n \\t}\\n-\\tmanifest, err := specpin.Verify(lockBytes)\\n+\\tmanifest, err := specpin.VerifyV060(lockBytes)\\n \\tif err != nil {\\n \\t\\treturn Report{}, fail(\\\"verify normative source lock: %v\\\", err)\\n \\t}\\n@@ -244,13 +244,28 @@ func verifyRepository(repository fs.FS, assignedSections []string) (Report, erro\\n \\t\\treturn Report{}, fail(\\\"generated catalog is stale; run go generate ./internal/catalog\\\")\\n \\t}\\n \\n-\\tcurrentCatalog, err := catalog.ForRelease(catalog.ReleaseV050)\\n+\\tcurrentCatalog, err := catalog.ForRelease(catalog.ReleaseV060)\\n \\tif err != nil {\\n \\t\\treturn Report{}, fail(\\\"load current catalog: %v\\\", err)\\n \\t}\\n \\tif err := verifyCatalogContracts(manifest.Contracts, currentCatalog.Contracts); err != nil {\\n \\t\\treturn Report{}, err\\n \\t}\\n+\\t// The legacy projection keeps the superseded v0.5.0 registry honest:\\n+\\t// the generated catalog must still carry the exact historical rows the\\n+\\t// adopted lock derives, so legacy support claims stay verifiable after\\n+\\t// the authority moved to v0.6.0.\\n+\\tlegacyContracts, err := manifest.ContractsForRelease(specpin.ReleaseV050)\\n+\\tif err != nil {\\n+\\t\\treturn Report{}, fail(\\\"derive legacy catalog contracts: %v\\\", err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tlegacyCatalog, err := catalog.ForRelease(catalog.ReleaseV050)\\n+\\tif err != nil {\\n+\\t\\treturn Report{}, fail(\\\"load legacy catalog: %v\\\", err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tif err := verifyCatalogContracts(legacyContracts, legacyCatalog.Contracts); err != nil {\\n+\\t\\treturn Report{}, err\\n+\\t}\\n \\tcompatibilityCatalog, err := catalog.ForRelease(catalog.ReleaseV043)\\n \\tif err != nil {\\n \\t\\treturn Report{}, fail(\\\"load compatibility catalog: %v\\\", err)\\n@@ -268,11 +283,11 @@ func verifyRepository(repository fs.FS, assignedSections []string) (Report, erro\\n \\tif err != nil {\\n \\t\\treturn Report{}, err\\n \\t}\\n-\\tdocument, err := specdoc.Load()\\n+\\tdocument, err := specdoc.LoadV060()\\n \\tif err != nil {\\n \\t\\treturn Report{}, fail(\\\"load pinned specification document: %v\\\", err)\\n \\t}\\n-\\tif manifest.Source.Document.SHA256 != specpin.DocumentSHA256 {\\n+\\tif manifest.Source.Document.SHA256 != specpin.DocumentSHA256V060 {\\n \\t\\treturn Report{}, fail(\\n \\t\\t\\t\\\"verified normative lock document digest %s differs from the pinned clause source %s\\\",\\n \\t\\t\\tmanifest.Source.Document.SHA256, specpin.DocumentSHA256)\\n@@ -629,8 +644,8 @@ func resolveAssignedSections(pinned []string, assigned []string) ([]assignedSect\\n \\t\\troot := canonical\\n \\t\\tidentifiers := []string{canonical}\\n \\t\\tif strings.HasPrefix(canonical, \\\"appendix-\\\") {\\n\\n- NOTE (pre-existing, not touched): README still says \\\"One admitted binding out of forty-nine\\\" while `tracecheck` measures `bindings=53` — stale since before this task (first run here already showed 53). Flagged for the review rather than fixed in passing.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/sessadapter/{census_test,probe,context,tuple}.go` + `probe_test.go` (bad status), `internal/traceability/{ownership.v0.5.0.json,traceability.go,traceability_test.go,cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go}`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry). Work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0 round 5: B4/B5 closed as classes by derived denominators, N8 indirection refused\\n- FIX (B8): `bound_census_test.go` rosters all 97 production bound sites (six helpers by member, len guards by shape with values normalized out, DecodeFindings cap instantiations): 82 driven at entries both edges, 15 exempt (4 mechanism, 4 plumbing, 3 equivalent, 5 stated-bound 65536-count rows). `requireStringBounds`/`requireUint53Bounds` wrappers are mechanism rows; the 19 caller sites carry the rows.\\n- FIX (B7): `identity_census_test.go` rosters all 62 `X != Y` gates (mechanical classes excluded) plus a 5-row presence census with structural proof: 54 driven zero-on-exempted-side at exported entries (CheckProbe x6 both sides, seal 8x2, admission key x5 entry+binding sides, binding caller-side x4), 8 exempt (2 dispatch, 4 sentinel, 2 equivalent).\\n- FIX (N8): `constructorSitesInFile` reports any `axerror.New` selector outside call-fun position; synthetic proof covers package-level and function-local indirection (report) vs definition spelling and Decode (exempt).\\n- FINDINGS (battery corrected the work, all in-session): `Bext-min` is genuinely equivalent (no 2-char key satisfies the reverse-DNS grammar); `Iops-candidate` is genuinely equivalent (both sides come from `requireDigestValue`); registry-element gates had no \\\"\\\" row (added `TestRegistryElementEmptyRefuses`); `Ituple-strategies` needed a struct-level [\\\"\\\"] row (added); `Ibind-tuple` first exempted the wrong side (context is never zero; corrected to the admitted side and killed). Len-guard census IDs briefly embedded values and caught a mutant statically — normalized to shape-only so values are pinned behaviorally, per the file's own documented design.\\n- EVIDENCE: battery `/tmp/battery.py`, 153 mutants applied by exact string, PRESENT-confirmed, restore-verified: 147 killed, 6 equivalent-confirmed (3 full-green, 3 behavioral-green with only the roster failing closed on the added clause), 0 survived, 0 not-applied. Additive probe file failed all three censuses naming the planted sites, then removed. Full table attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-table-rev5.md`.\\n- SCOPE: test files only (`bound_census_test.go`, `identity_census_test.go`, `inventory_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `zero_absent_test.go`); zero production changes, so no resurrections possible. `go test ./...` 17/17 green, `-cover` green (sessadapter 82.4%), `-race` green on the package, vet + gofmt clean.\\n- STATUS: handed to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0 round 7: rev6 G-B closed — shape space enumerated per census, three shapes derived, residue bounded\\n- FIX (identity): `identityGatesInSyntax` now derives `bytes.Equal` calls and visits package-level var initializers under their variable name (same scope rule as the constructor census; per-scope ordinals keep all existing rows identical). One live row added: `context.go|CheckContextEcho|bytes.Equal(received.raw, sent.raw)` (domain `context-echo`, driver `TestCheckContextEcho`) — the live instance rev6 named. Header enumerates 8 identity-decision shapes (7 derived, 1 bound: other stdlib predicates) and qualifies the census sentence to derived shapes.\\n- FIX (bound): `boundSitesInSyntax` visits package-level var initializers and derives guards over length variables bound directly from `len(...)`/`stringLength(...)` (parens/conversions unwrap; `values := make(..., len(x))` binds no variable — proven by synthetic negative), plus direct `stringLength(...)` comparisons. Four live mechanism half-rows added (checkStringBounds + checkSortedUniqueStrings enforcements, exempt with caller-row drivers). Header enumerates 10 bound shapes (6 derived, 2 stated-pinned, 2 bounded: decoded-value comparisons with live checkUint53Bounds:269, direct cap/RuneCount with none live) and folds in the 21 refusal-side-only drivers instead of claiming min/max admission per site.\\n- FIX (constructor): no derivation change (7/7 already); header enumerates the 7 construction shapes with residue (frameFault-via-alias, non-Go construction, out-of-dir/_test.go), plus synthetic proofs for failX in return/argument/struct-field positions and returned `axerror.New`.\\n- FINDINGS (battery corrected the work, all in-session): the first length-var rule (RHS subtree contains len) over-derived on `values := make([]T, 0, len(elements))`, claiming element sortedness checks as len sites — tightened to direct binding; the P7 switch-arm plant kills at the arm witness entry, not the switch census (statement-vs-arm division of labor, now stated in the header); capability-clause and mechanism-comparison narrowings always co-fire their census by exact-render design — reported as behavioural kills with expected co-fire, never as clean singles.\\n- EVIDENCE: 15-row battery, 6 behavioural kills (incl. echo same-length narrowing failing `TestCheckContextEcho`, mechanism max+1 failing 5 bound suites, conditional-at-write-gate failing `TestCheckTargetWriteGatesRefusesNonAvailableEnabled`), 6 census-only kills (all three rev6 plant shapes now redden), 3 stated survivors green (plain-param bound, cap, reflect.DeepEqual). Tables attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-table-rev7.md`, narrative as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_rework-evidence-rev7.md`.\\n- SCOPE: test files only (`identity_census_test.go`, `bound_census_test.go`, `inventory_test.go`) + LOGBOOK.md (this entry); zero production changes. `go test ./...` 17/17 green, vet + GOOS=windows vet + gofmt clean, `-race` green, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=88). Census counts: identity 100 (86/14), bound 107 (80/27), constructors 7; test inventory 109->111 (+2 synthetic, 0 removed).\\n- STATUS: handed to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 13196,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 3299,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
