hed in behavior.\\n- DELTA (measured, SPEC §1.5 cross-checked row-for-row in order): +Session selector `urn:ax:contract:session-selector` 1.0.0, +Host Channel `urn:ax:transport:host-channel` 1.0.0, +Host Trust Store 1.0.0; Configuration +4.0.0, Mesh RPC +5.0.0, Structured error +1.4.0, CLI result +5.0.0; +13 sections (6.6, 11.10.x6, 14.7.x6), normative scope still 24; +2 fixtures (host-channel `20aa66c3…`, selector `2bda47f5…`), 3 old fixture files byte-identical upstream. Selector fixture ID is pin-local (`ax-session-selector-conformance-v1`, path-stem convention — upstream file carries `specification_version`/`contract`, no `fixture` discriminator); host-channel ID matches the upstream discriminator.\\n- HISTORY: v0.6.0 projections of v0.5.0 (60 rows) and v0.4.3 (55 rows) are `reflect.DeepEqual` to the real v0.5.0 lock and its projection — adoption cannot rewrite history. `ContractsForRelease(v0.6.0)` on a v0.5.0 manifest is refused: a stale pin cannot authorize the new release. New runtime contracts (selector/auth) are pinned only; no `ax` surface claims them.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2154,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 539,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
